 ## Overview
-Multi-view Color Consistency and Smoothing is a post-processing method for assigning colors to voxels in a fine volumetric reconstruction, designed to compensate for noise arising from camera calibration, imaging artifacts, imperfect light balance, and volume quantization [S1, S2]. It distinguishes itself from basic voxel coloring by explicitly handling non-Lambertian reflectance and preventing visual blurring through a "blur group" mechanism that preserves sharp edges [S1, S2]. It builds on [Voxel Coloring](4418-voxel-coloring.md) by refining the color attributes of already-identified surface voxels.
